        <item>
            <title>0.8.5</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 19:46:19 +0200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1791222224</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## Changed

- **Smoother Cmd+scroll zoom.** Zooming with Cmd and the trackpad or mouse wheel now glides in even steps at every screen refresh instead of following each input event. The difference is largest on 60 Hz external displays, where trackpad zoom used to stall on some frames and jump on others.
  - A notched mouse wheel glides each notch instead of jumping 7 % in one frame, and a fast spin no longer races to the size limit.
  - A run of wheel notches resizes the terminal once, when you stop, instead of after every notch, which removes a short hitch per notch.
- New app icon, with a larger prompt and keys so it stays legible at Dock and Finder sizes.

## Fixed

- Lifting and re-touching the trackpad in the middle of a Cmd+scroll zoom no longer snaps the text back to the size it started at for a frame.
- After an external display is disconnected, Laban no longer stays stuck at that display's refresh rate on the built-in screen (for example 60 Hz on a 120 Hz MacBook Pro panel) until it is restarted.
]]></description>
